The dirent buffer is variable-length records packed together.
Walk it with a byte offset, casting to struct linux_dirent64 at each position.
Advance by d_reclen, not by sizeof.

When you remove a record, memmove everything after it backward by d_reclen
bytes.
Subtract d_reclen from your total count but do not advance your offset, because
the next record is now at the current position.

For PID hiding, /proc has one directory per PID.
The d_name is the PID as a decimal string.
Compare it against your pid_targets the same way you compare file names against
file_targets.
